# DEFERRED ON COST 2026-08-24 (Ray's ruling, and the reason `build = defer`
# exists at all — see `kb_setup.manifest.Manifest.build`).
#
# NOT a defect. This source is healthy and would extract fine; it is simply the
# most expensive item on the migration list and the least obviously a Claude
# source. Measured at registration: 1,551 `.org` files against 7 `.md`, 342 MB,
# GitHub reports the language as HTML. `.org` IS in graphify's `_PROSE_EXTS`
# (`sources/graphify/graphify/detect.py:185`), so every one of those 1,551 files
# would go through `--mode deep` as prose — roughly 29% of the whole four-source
# claude prose load, for a Hacker News reading archive rather than Claude
# documentation.
#
# WHAT WOULD CLEAR THIS — and this is the field's whole point, because it is not
# "someone fixes something": a cheaper extraction backend (graphify PR #2981's
# `openai-cli`, pinned in this repo's fork), a decision that the HN discussions
# are worth their spend, or a scoping rule that takes a subset rather than all
# 1,551 files. Any of the three is a BUDGET answer, not a repair.
#
# The pin above stays committed and fingerprinted either way: this is an
# exclusion from the build, never from the record (Invariant 3).
build = defer
defer_reason = Ray 2026-08-24: 1,551 .org files (~29% of the four-source claude prose load) for an HN reading archive, not Claude docs. Clears on a cheaper backend, a ruling that it is worth the spend, or a subsetting rule — not on a fix
